==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*8 [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[Sir Seal]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
At first glance, this stage seems like a pushover. That is, until you realize that the Sir Seal is buffed to a whopping 10,000% on {{1c}}. At this magnification, Sir Seal has 250,000 health and deals 15,000 damage. Your meatshields will have too little health to withstand a hit, so it is best to opt for [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-Controller]]s instead: [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Sorceress Cat]], [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Captain Cat]], [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Face Cat]], and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] are all useful here. In other words, treat the Sir Seal like you would a [[Bore]].

*If you have trouble killing the Mooths, it is recommended to use [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] cats like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]] or cats that outrange them like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]].
*Unlike a Bore, Sir Seal only has one knockback. This makes pure damage even less effective at taking it down.

